  "raw": {
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4636": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Hockey Operations",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Coordinator of Hockey Operations Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Coordinator of Hockey Operations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the application. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Franco Bari, Director of Intercollegiate Athletics, fbari@stlawu.edu. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Coordinator of Hockey Operations FLSA Exempt Primary Responsibilities St. Lawrence University is now accepting applications for the coordinator of hockey operations. This is a full-time, 9-month, position. The director of hockey ops will be responsible for coordinating the operational aspect of men’s and women’s hockey including video operations, on-ice duties per NCAA rules and regulations, other administrative duties as assigned. Primary Responsibilities: Communicate with hockey operations platforms to maintain and upgrade servers/computers and for high-working efficiencies Research, select and provide pre-scout video clips of opponents during pre-game team meetings to identify strengths & weaknesses of the opponent Breakdown of daily practice video for team/individual performance improvement Assure compliance with NCAA / ECAC rules regarding video exchange Hire, train and supervise hockey programs internal video camera operators for all home games and practices Prepare ice for practices: identifies and secures needed equipment & resources Administer alumni, recruits and roster platforms Work with coaching staff for coordinating and logging academic, athletic and team schedules Oversee and coordinates with student assistants for men’s and women’s programs Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required Hockey operations/video coordinator experience preferred Demonstrated ability in the use of various software in the industry Ability to effectively communicate with faculty/staff, University community members and alumni Knowledge of all NCAA and ECAC rules & regulations pertaining to DI M & W hockey preferred Must have a philosophy compatible with highly selective academic standards within a Liberal Arts University and the mission of St. Lawrence University. Preferred Qualifications Salary $46,765 Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) FT Seasonal Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01546 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicant Please complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the application. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Franco Bari, Director of Intercollegiate Athletics, fbari@stlawu.edu. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree or higher? Yes No * Do you hold a valid driver's license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Contact Information for 3 Professional References Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4619": {
      "title": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | General Laborer Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers General Laborer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. SLU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Posting Details Position Information Position Title General Laborer FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Responsibilities Performs work required in the care, maintenance, cleaning and housekeeping of university buildings and campus in accordance with established practices and procedures. Responsible for performing duties associated with setups and deliveries for special events in and around all campus buildings. In the absence of the material recycler or supply clerk performs the regular duties of that position as assigned. As required performs the primary duties of other “A” classification personnel as assigned by the Management staff. Schedule: Sunday- Thursday 7am -3:30pm flexible schedule Days off: Friday and Saturday Location: Sykes and as assigned. Minimum Qualifications High School diploma (or equivalent) required. Ability to follow verbal and printed instructions. The ability to prepare or verbalize reports necessary to the position. Requires ability to lift a minimum of 45 lbs., bending, climbing, pushing, and pulling. Must be able to meet University requirements to be authorized to drive University vehicles as assigned. Preferred Qualifications Previous Cleaning experience Salary SEIU Level A: $16.00 to $21.38/hr. The actual compensation will be determined based on experience and other factors permitted by law. Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) Full-time (12 months) Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01488 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Please complete the online application form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. SLU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application References Optional Documents Reference Letters 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
