    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4588": {
      "title": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Head Coach - Women&#39;s Triathlon Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Head Coach - Women's Triathlon Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested and qualified applicants please complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Franco Bari, Director of Intercollegiate Athletics, fbari@stlawu.edu. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully completing a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Head Coach - Women's Triathlon FLSA Exempt Primary Responsibilities St. Lawrence University invites applications for a Head Coach for Women’s Triathlon. The head coach will direct the development, organization and management of all phases of this Division III Women’s Triathlon program. Primarily responsible for the instruction of athletes both on and off the field and in the classroom, organization, administration, coaching and recruitment. Candidates must possess a strong commitment to the academic mission of the University and to a competitive NCAA Division III Athletics Program. Primary Responsibilities: Management of all phases of a DIII women’s triathlon program Direct student-athlete development both on and off the field; ensuring academic success, good citizenship, sportsmanship, and promotion of positive values consistent with the mission of St. Lawrence University Recruitment of highly qualified student-athletes Program organization; including practice planning, game preparation, and systems implementation for both offense and defense Ability to supervise, evaluate, and effectively provide direction to one graduate assistant coach Additional responsibilities include a secondary assignment such as game management, intramurals or teaching in the minor, as well as other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Any combination equivalent to a bachelor’s degree and three years of proven success as a coach of a club, high school, or intercollegiate triathlon program. Demonstrated ability to recruit diverse, quality student-athletes Ability to effectively communicate with student-athletes, faculty/staff, University community members and alumni Knowledge of all NCAA and USA Triathlon rules & regulations pertaining to DIII women’s triathlon. The candidate must have the ability to understand the needs of students, colleagues, and communities from diverse backgrounds, identities and intersections. They must demonstrate a distinct commitment to creating an equitable and welcoming environment. Ability to meet University requirements to drive a University vehicle required. Preferred Qualifications Salary $62,353.20 Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) Full-time (12 months) Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01532 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Interested and qualified applicants please complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Franco Bari, Director of Intercollegiate Athletics, fbari@stlawu.edu. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully completing a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree or higher? Yes No * Do you hold a valid driver's license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Contact Information for 3 Professional References Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
