    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4541": {
      "title": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Skilled Trades- Boiler Tender Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Skilled Trades- Boiler Tender Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application form and include contact information for at least three professional references. All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Skilled Trades- Boiler Tender FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Responsibilities Operate high/medium/low pressure boilers. Maintain and operate all equipment in the heating plant as directed. Install, maintain, adjust, modify and perform major overhaul and repair of heating, ventilating, and air conditioning systems by interpreting blueprints, manufacturer specifications, written and verbal instructions. Apply thorough knowledge of one or more of the accepted trades with a basic knowledge of three others. Applicable trades include carpenter, painter, electrician, plumber, fleet mechanic, boiler tender, HVAC Technician. Apply skill in the use of tools and equipment and be responsible for tools, materials, and devices to perform tasks according to accepted practices. Perform related duties as required to accomplish tasks. DUTIES PERFORMED : In addition to the requirements for personal conduct, which are common to all positions in the University, the following duties outline the major factors of the position. They are not all inclusive, do not set priority sequence, or establish a ration for work to be performed. They may vary in importance and may be altered within the general framework of the Primary Function to satisfy changes in department activity. Operation of high/medium/low pressure boilers Regulation of central heating system steam flow Cleans, lubricates and maintains equipment Reads gauges, charts, and cleans and maintains same Operates and maintains the water make-up system, including daily testing as required Inspection of pumps and motors Performs the work in the operation of the steam generating plant Operation of steam turbine and electrical generation system Operation of energy management systems Perform daily and all other routine building maintenance and housekeeping as required Performs other duties as required Schedule: The work schedule is a flexible, rotating schedule Location: Central Heating Plant Minimum Qualifications Education: High School diploma (or equivalent) required. Experience: Two (2) years of experience in journeyman trades level work is required. May consider specific coursework related to this position toward the journeyman trades experience along with other professional trades work experience. Preference for work experience with high and low pressure boilers. Skills Required: Ability and willingness to follow routine verbal and written instructions. Ability to verbalize or write reports/forms necessary to the job. Valid drivers license. Must be able to meet University requirements to be authorized to drive University vehicles. Required operation of equipment related to the trade. Required bending, heavy lifting, climbing ladders and stairs. Preferred Qualifications Associates degree in HVAC Technology, Electrical Technology or Mechanical Technology. Salary $19.78-$28.09/hr. Level E SEIU The actual compensation will be determined based on experience and other factors permitted by law. Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) Full-time (12 months) Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01503 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Please complete the online application form and include contact information for at least three professional references. All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4006": {
      "title": "University Driver (temporary position)",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | University Driver (temporary position) Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers University Driver (temporary position) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application form and include contact information for professional references. Upload a cover letter and resume in the Applicant Documents section of the application form. Offers are conditioned upon successful completion of a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title University Driver (temporary position) FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Responsibilities Operates a vehicle/van safely and efficiently. Follows specific regularly scheduled routes, charter routes or responds to requests from the Transportation Coordinator, dispatch or management for unscheduled pick ups or drop offs. Assists the passengers in boarding and exiting vehicle. Loads and unloads luggage, packages and other items. Reports any vehicle accidents or other safety situations to the dispatch center immediately. Inspects exterior and interior of vehicle at beginning of each shift for properly operating headlights, turn signals, brake lights, interior courtesy lamps, checks fluids, air-conditioning or heating, warning lamps, mirror adjustment, properly inflated tires, windshield wipers, vehicle damage, etc. prior to moving vehicle. Responsible for ensuring inside and outside of vehicle are properly cleaned and fueled on an ongoing basis. Keeps interior of vehicle neat and orderly. Monitors vehicle condition and records malfunctioning items or damage and notifies the dispatch center to have a work order submitted. Accurately completes driver trip sheet for each shift with information including driver’s name, vehicle number, number of passengers, pick up and drop off times, mileages, fares, destinations, etc. Records passenger name and university ID number. Customer service skills that respectfully communicate with passengers in a courteous, friendly and professional manner. Perform all other related duties as assigned. This is a Temporary position The pay rate is $15/hour. Minimum Qualifications Must be 21 years of age or older and meet university requirements for driving a university vehicle. Must possess a valid Driver’s License ( CDL License preferred) with no convictions or at-fault accidents, DWAI , DWI , or DUI convictions within the last year. Work experience in a driving or related position preferred. Preferred Qualifications Prior professional driving experience. Salary $15.50/hr. Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) Temporary Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01269 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Please complete the online application form and include contact information for professional references. Upload a cover letter and resume in the Applicant Documents section of the application form. Offers are conditioned upon successful completion of a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
