    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4554": {
      "title": "Bookstore Assistant Director",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Bookstore Assistant Director Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Bookstore Assistant Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested and qualified candidates should complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Lyndon Lake, Bookstore Director, llake@stlawu.edu. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Bookstore Assistant Director FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Responsibilities The Assistant Director of the Bookstore is responsible for assisting in the general management of the Bookstore. Responsibilities include supervision of operations and staff, training, scheduling, administering student employee scheduling and payroll and managing workflow. Enhance and support purchasing operations making recommendations and decisions. Respond courteously to customer inquiries. Prepare reports, assist with inventory planning and execution, promote sales events, orders, supplies and related retail and administrative duties. The person in the position will perform store opening and closing duties and hours of work vary and include weekends. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Primary Supervisor for day-to-day front-end management of Bookstore Recruit, train and schedule Bookstore and student staff. Update, develop and implement a formalized training program for all students, including customer service training, PCI training and general training of Bookstore systems and processes. Assist with strategizing, execution and advertising on- and off-site store sales events. Strategize workflow and assist with managing staff during peak periods. Assist with procedure development, implementation, and enforcement. Respond to customer inquiries as they arise. Confer with department clerks regarding issues, opportunities and goals in their respective areas. Prepare various reports to inform decision-making as needed. Be available to perform store closing and opening duties several days per week as seasonal schedules dictate. Oversees inventory management, including conducting periodic cycle counts and verifications to ensure accuracy. Performs inventory control though cycle counts and working with buyers on any negative on hands. Confirms proper entry, removal, and recording of merchandise in the inventory system. Assists in leading the annual inventory process. Provide backup to Bookstore AP Clerk Position as needed. Backup duties to all staff as needed. Standard Sales Associate Duties (expected of all Bookstore personnel) Provide the highest level of customer service; ensure proper quality control of merchandise, maintain forms and cash levels, keep checkout area neat and orderly. Maintain secure point-of-sale and monitor security system. Respond to customer needs, box or wrap merchandise, promote good will between store/University and the customer/public. Provide first line sales floor security: Maintain awareness of potential shop lifting, respond to perceived shop lifting activities, respond to security gate alarms. Cashier Support: Oversee, train, and support student employees while working at cash registers and the front service desk. Train full-time employees on the operation of the POS and cashier processes. Shipping/Receiving: Provide backup and assistance with preparing shipments and appropriate documentation for returns, mail orders, and other shipments. Minimum Qualifications Associate’s degree in related field and at least 3 years management/supervisory experience in a retail setting. Equivalent combinations of education and experience will be considered for those with extensive relevant retail management experience. Demonstrated ability to lead and motivate employees toward a common goal. A track record of fostering positive change and delivering favorable outcomes, the ability to produce quantitative analysis, both operationally and financially and the acumen to navigate a complex work environment. Knowledge of merchandising, advertising, marketing, promotion, and display. Technology Broad, very strong, technology background required with experience working in a technology driven work environment. Detailed knowledge of retail operations including retail accounting systems/procedures, electronic Point-of-Sale/inventory. Experience training and supporting employees in the use of technology. Experience creating reports and analyzing data. Proficiency with Microsoft Excel and experience with other Microsoft Office Applications. Required Skills Excellent leadership and collaboration skills. Excellent organizational skills with precise attention to detail required and the highest quality standards. Strong communication skills required, including oral, written, and listening skills. Demonstrable good judgment and the ability to work under pressure. Must be a well-organized, high-energy individual with excellent customer service skills. Must be able to set priorities, make decisions and work independently and as part of a team. Proven ability to develop positive and productive working relationships. Experience with customer service standards and procedures. Preferred Qualifications Experience in the college bookstore industry. Experience developing innovative programs and services. Salary $25.00 - $27.50 per hour. The start rate will be determined by skills, experience, and other factors permitted by law. Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) Full-time (12 months) Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01518 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Interested and qualified candidates should complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Lyndon Lake, Bookstore Director, llake@stlawu.edu. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Other Document 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4449": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant Coach",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant Coach - Men&#39;s &amp; Women&#39;s Nordic Ski Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Graduate Assistant Coach - Men's & Women's Nordic Ski Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates should submit a letter of application, resume, and contact information for 3 professional references. These documents can be uploaded in the “Applicant Documents” section of your application. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Ethan Townsend, Head Coach, at etownsend@stlawu.edu. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Assistant Coach - Men's & Women's Nordic Ski FLSA Exempt Primary Responsibilities St. Lawrence University is currently seeking applications for a Graduate Assistant Coach for Men’s & Women’s Nordic Ski. This is a 9-month position (August 2026 – May 2027) targeted toward graduate students seeking a master’s degree. Remuneration includes a competitive coaching stipend, student health insurance, and eligibility for tuition remission (6 graduate classes per year in the University’s graduate program). St Lawrence offers a Master of Arts in Leadership. Duties/Responsibilities Responsibilities include providing instruction and  assisting with the day-to-day operation of the program including but not limited to athlete development, social media, recruiting, equipment management, travel, technique feedback, and other administrative duties. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree is required Strong oral and written communication skills Valid driver’s license and ability to meet the requirements to drive University vehicles required. Must apply and be accepted into the graduate program at St. Lawrence University. Preferred Qualifications Collegiate playing and/or coaching experience preferred. Salary $888 biweekly Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) FT Seasonal Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01477 Desired Start Date 08/10/2026 Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Candidates should submit a letter of application, resume, and contact information for 3 professional references. These documents can be uploaded in the “Applicant Documents” section of your application. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Ethan Townsend, Head Coach, at etownsend@stlawu.edu. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree or higher? Yes No * Do you hold a valid driver's license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Contact Information for 3 Professional References Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4634": {
      "title": "Viebranz Visiting Professor of Creative Writing",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Viebranz Visiting Professor of Creative Writing Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Viebranz Visiting Professor of Creative Writing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested and qualified applicants should submit a detailed letter of application, C.V. emphasizing publications and relevant teaching experience, sample syllabi and a writing sample of no more than 15 pages. These documents should be uploaded in the “Applicant Documents” section of the candidate’s application. Additionally, three confidential letters of reference are required [the required information input in the reference contact information section of your application will be utilized to send a system-derived email requesting a recommendation letter from each reference]. Applications should be received by October 16, 2026; review will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position can be directed to Professor Caroline Breashears, Search Chair at cbreashears@stlawu.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Viebranz Visiting Professor of Creative Writing FLSA Exempt Primary Responsibilities Creative writers with significant publications and teaching experience are invited to apply for the position of Viebranz Visiting Professor of Creative Writing for the academic years 2027-2028 through 2028-2029. Publications and teaching experience in creative nonfiction and another genre are preferable. The individual hired will teach two genre-specific courses each semester at the beginning or advanced level and be an active participant in the English Department. Departmental activities will include the following in each year of the appointment: giving a reading as part of the St. Lawrence University Writers Series, possibly serving as a reader on a senior honors thesis or directing a senior independent project, and leading occasional workshops for senior writing majors and/or giving a craft talk on writing. Evidence will be sought of a proven record of innovative pedagogy in creative writing and an enthusiasm for teaching. The successful candidate will join a department with a curricular commitment to teaching the mutuality of the study of literature and the practice of creative expression. A fully furnished house is provided as part of the compensation package. Minimum Qualifications M.F.A. or Ph.D. with creative dissertation, at least two books published by contract start date, and significant additional publications are required. Minimum of two years of undergraduate teaching experience required. Preferred Qualifications Salary $90,000 annually Faculty Status Visiting Assistant Professor Appointment Timing Full Year Posting Detail Information Posting Number FA00228 Desired Start Date 08/17/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Interested and qualified applicants should submit a detailed letter of application, C.V. emphasizing publications and relevant teaching experience, sample syllabi and a writing sample of no more than 15 pages. These documents should be uploaded in the “Applicant Documents” section of the candidate’s application. Additionally, three confidential letters of reference are required [the required information input in the reference contact information section of your application will be utilized to send a system-derived email requesting a recommendation letter from each reference]. Applications should be received by October 16, 2026; review will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position can be directed to Professor Caroline Breashears, Search Chair at cbreashears@stlawu.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Reference Requests Reference Request Details Accept References Yes Minimum Requests 3 Maximum Requests 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Sample Syllabus Writing Sample Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
