    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4615": {
      "title": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Facilities Custodial Manager Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Facilities Custodial Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested and qualified candidates should complete the online application form and upload the required documents in the “Applicant Documents” section of the application. Professional reference contact information should be provided in the application form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Marijo Haggett, Associate Vice President of Facilities & Dining Services via e-mail mlhaggett@stlawu or by phone (315) 229 5982 All offers are contingent upon successful completion of a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Facilities Custodial Manager FLSA Exempt Primary Responsibilities The Facilities Custodial Manager provides daily leadership for custodial operations and building stewardship within assigned campus areas. This entry-level management position directly supervises bargaining-unit and other assigned staff, ensures established service and cleanliness standards are met, and serves as a primary Facilities contact for building occupants. Reporting to the Assistant Director of Custodial Services, the manager coordinates building needs with Skilled Trades, Grounds, the Heating Plant, and other Facilities groups and serves as a liaison with campus departments, including Residence Life. Essential Responsibilities Custodial Operations and Staff Leadership Plan, schedule, assign, inspect, and document custodial work to maintain clean, healthy, safe, and welcoming buildings. Develop staffing plans, coverage schedules, and daily and periodic task assignments based on building use and institutional priorities. Monitor performance against departmental standards, address deficiencies promptly, and follow through until work is complete. Directly supervise assigned custodians, cleaners, general laborers, temporary employees, summer employees, and student employees or lead roles, as applicable. Manage schedules, attendance, timekeeping, payroll review, leave, overtime, onboarding, training, performance reviews, coaching, and employee development. Address performance and workplace concerns consistently and with appropriate documentation. Consult with the Assistant Director, Facilities leadership, and Human Resources regarding recruitment, hiring, discipline, termination, and other significant personnel actions in accordance with University policy and the collective bargaining agreement. Maintain custodial supplies and equipment, promote safe work practices, and provide hands-on instruction or operational support when needed. Building Stewardship and Campus Coordination Serve as the building manager and primary Facilities contact for assigned areas and as a liaison with campus departments, including Residence Life, faculty, staff, students, student leaders, and event coordinators. Maintain regular visibility in assigned buildings, identify emerging concerns, and communicate safety, access, service, and operational needs to the appropriate staff. Enter and track accurate work orders and coordinate with Skilled Trades, Grounds, the Heating Plant, and other Facilities groups to address building needs and support timely follow-through. Coordinate custodial access and service around classes, residential needs, special events, construction, and other campus operations. Respond professionally to questions and concerns and communicate status, delays, or unresolved issues through the appropriate channels. Budget, Planning, and Campus Readiness Operate within assigned budgets; monitor payroll, overtime, temporary labor, supplies, equipment, and contracted services; and review purchases within delegated authority. Assist the Assistant Director with annual budgets, staffing projections, equipment replacement plans, custodial capital requests, and operational reporting. Provide observations about building conditions and feedback from occupants to support broader Facilities and capital planning. Plan custodial staffing and readiness for student arrival and departure, summer programs, Commencement, Reunion, athletics, conferences, and other campus events. Work a schedule that may vary based on operational needs and support assigned on-call, evening, weekend, weather, event, and emergency-response responsibilities. Perform other related duties consistent with the role and the operational needs of the University. Supervisory Scope Direct supervision of assigned bargaining-unit custodial employees and other temporary, summer, or student staff. The manager may coordinate the work of outside contractors and works across Facilities groups and campus departments to coordinate building needs, access, communication, and follow-through. Minimum Qualifications Associates degree and at least three years related work experience required. May consider an equivalent amount of education and experience and at least two years related work experience and at least one year of supervisory experience in a related field. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively, organize competing priorities, address service concerns, exercise sound judgment, and work successfully with employees and campus constituents. Ability to use or promptly learn email, work-order, payroll/timekeeping, and standard office systems. Preferred Qualifications Experience in a unionized workplace or working under a collective bargaining agreement. Experience in a college, university, school, healthcare, hospitality, or similarly complex multi-building environment. Experience with custodial standards, safety practices, budgets, work-order systems, or event support. Associate degree or higher in facilities management, business, hospitality, public administration, or a related field. Salary $62,353.20 - $67,000 Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) Full-time (12 months) Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01544 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Interested and qualified candidates should complete the online application form and upload the required documents in the “Applicant Documents” section of the application. Professional reference contact information should be provided in the application form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Marijo Haggett, Associate Vice President of Facilities & Dining Services via e-mail mlhaggett@stlawu or by phone (315) 229 5982 All offers are contingent upon successful completion of a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have an Associate’s degree and at least three years related work experience? (Open Ended Question) How many years experience do you have supervising or managing people? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4587": {
      "title": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Head Coach - Women&#39;s Flag Football Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Head Coach - Women's Flag Football Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested and qualified applicants please complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Franco Bari, Director of Intercollegiate Athletics, fbari@stlawu.edu. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully completing a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Head Coach - Women's Flag Football FLSA Exempt Primary Responsibilities St. Lawrence University invites applications for a Head Coach for Women’s Flag Football. The head coach will direct the development, organization and management of all phases of this Division III Women’s Flag Football program. Primarily responsible for the instruction of athletes both on and off the field and in the classroom, organization, administration, coaching and recruitment. Candidates must possess a strong commitment to the academic mission of the University and to a competitive NCAA Division III Athletics Program. Primary Responsibilities: Management of all phases of a DIII women’s flag football program Direct student-athlete development both on and off the field; ensuring academic success, good citizenship, sportsmanship, and promotion of positive values consistent with the mission of St. Lawrence University Recruitment of highly qualified student-athletes Program organization; including practice planning, game preparation, and systems implementation for both offense and defense Ability to supervise, evaluate, and effectively provide direction to one graduate assistant coach Additional responsibilities include a secondary assignment such as game management, intramurals or teaching in the minor, as well as other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Any combination equivalent to a bachelor’s degree and three years of proven success as a coach of a club, high school, or intercollegiate flag football program. Demonstrated ability to recruit diverse, quality student-athletes Ability to effectively communicate with student-athletes, faculty/staff, University community members and alumni Knowledge of all NCAA and conference affiliated rules & regulations pertaining to DIII women’s flag football. The candidate must have the ability to understand the needs of students, colleagues, and communities from diverse backgrounds, identities and intersections. They must demonstrate a distinct commitment to creating an equitable and welcoming environment. Ability to meet University requirements to drive a University vehicle required. Preferred Qualifications Salary $62,353.20 annually Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) Full-time (12 months) Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01533 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicant Interested and qualified applicants please complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Franco Bari, Director of Intercollegiate Athletics, fbari@stlawu.edu. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully completing a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree or higher? Yes No * Do you hold a valid driver's license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Contact Information for 3 Professional References Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4532": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant Coach",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant Coach - Men&#39;s &amp; Women&#39;s Tennis Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Graduate Assistant Coach - Men's & Women's Tennis Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested and qualified applicants should complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Assistant Coach - Men's & Women's Tennis FLSA Exempt Primary Responsibilities St. Lawrence University is currently seeking applicants for a Graduate Assistant Coach for Men’s & Women’s Tennis to begin Fall 2026. This 9-month position (August to May) is targeted toward graduate students seeking a master’s degree. Remuneration includes a very competitive coaching stipend, student health insurance, and eligibility for tuition remission (6 graduate classes per year in the University’s graduate program). St Lawrence offers a Master of Arts in Leadership. Duties/Responsibilities Responsibilities include providing instruction; assisting in practice preparation, match day duties, recruiting, and administrative tasks as assigned by the Head Coach. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree is required. Strong oral and written communication skills are necessary. A valid driver’s license and ability to meet the requirements to drive University vehicles required. Must apply and be accepted in the graduate program at St. Lawrence University. Preferred Qualifications Collegiate playing and/or coaching experience preferred. Salary $888 biweekly stipend, plus Tuition Remission (6 graduate classes per year in the University’s graduate program) Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) FT Seasonal Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01511 Desired Start Date 08/10/2026 Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Interested and qualified applicants should complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree or higher? Yes No * Do you hold a valid driver's license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume A List of 3 Professional References Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
