    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4637": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager of Equipment Operations",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Manager of Equipment Operations Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Assistant Manager of Equipment Operations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application form and upload required documents in the \"applicant documents\" section of the application form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Manager of Equipment Operations FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Responsibilities St. Lawrence University invites applications for an Assistant Manager of Equipment Operations. Under the direct supervision of the Associate Director of Operations responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, primary equipment manager for football, game day setup and breakdown for a variety of athletic teams, maintain and repair equipment, assist with work order submittal, laundry, oversee student workers and other duties as assigned. This is a part-time, 10 month, seasonal position in our Athletics department. Minimum Qualifications This position requires a minimum of a Bachelor’s degree or several years of experience in a related field. The candidate must demonstrate strong communication skills, have the ability to act with initiative, and to be able to work effectively with staff, faculty, and other members of the University community. A valid driver’s license and ability to meet the requirements to drive University vehicles required. The ability to work evenings, weekends and travel may be required. Preferred Qualifications Candidate is athletic equipment managers association certified ( AEMA ) or be willing to get certified within one (1) year. Salary $20 per hour Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) PT Seasonal Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01547 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Please complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the application form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold a valid driver's license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Contact Information for 3 Professional References Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4621": {
      "title": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Principal Clerk Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Principal Clerk Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete application form and include contact information for at least three professional work references. Upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section. All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Principal Clerk FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Responsibilities Reporting to the Director of Admissions Information Systems, the Principal Clerk, Admissions Front Desk/Reception will support the work of many aspects of the admissions process at St. Lawrence University, including recruitment, visitor experience management, event support, and daily scheduling. This position will have varied primary duties along with responsibilities shared with other members of the operations team. The position may require overtime work at various points during the year. The successful candidate will possess strong communication, customer service, organization and time management skills. They will exhibit professionalism, good judgment, knowledge of when to ask clarifying questions, and a desire for continuous improvement in their assigned duties. Regular hours will be Monday – Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. (12-month position). This position will also work closely with the Executive Director of Admissions. Duties Visitor Experience and Reception Maintain a welcoming, inviting lobby environment by keeping the space tidy, organizing materials, and maintaining the hospitality and refreshment station for visitors Check in visitors, including prospective students and families, alumni, school counselors, and other stakeholders Create individualized itineraries for visitors who request additional experiences, i.e. meeting with a professor or coach, sitting in on a class, or connecting with a current student Maintain visit records in Slate CRM , and ensure timely updates of registration status Order pub cookies for campus visitors and coordinate with dining services for pick up Create welcome packets, generate welcome letters and nametags, and finalize other preparations for daily campus visitors Monitor and respond to SMS (text) messages in the Front Desk inbox in Slate CRM Monitor inventory and order additional supplies for the hospitality area in the main lobby (consumables, paper products, etc.) Daily Schedule Support Align the shared admissions calendar with the Slate appointment calendar Enter all upcoming visits into Slate CRM , including tours, interviews, web interviews, and other events as needed and as determined by the Executive Director of Admissions Coordinate with admissions counseling staff and senior fellows for interview coverage and flow Generate daily visit lists for staff and student worker use Events Support Generate registration lists, nametags, signage, placards, and other materials for events Put together welcome bags with information for on-campus events Assist the Assistant Director for Admissions Events with event creation in Slate CRM Assist the Assistant Director for Admissions Events with room reservations, catering orders, and other event tasks Order printed materials, such as event schedules, from Office Services Student Worker Supervision & Support Coordinate daily tour assignments for admissions ambassadors and help to monitor their check-in and check-out process throughout the day Supervise the work of admissions clerical assistants while working at the front desk Approve hours for admissions ambassadors on a bi-weekly basis for payroll Work closely with the Ambassador Coordinator team to maintain expectations and enforce standards for the admissions ambassadors, especially during counselor travel General Operations Duties Data entry of inquiry cards or walk-in visitor cards, or through phone calls with potential campus visitors Monitor and resolve issues with bad addresses in Slate Monitor and resolve duplicate records in Slate Answer the main admissions line and forward calls appropriately (shared responsibility with operations staff and executive secretary) Monitor the main admissions email account, forward messages appropriately, and respond to messages as needed (shared responsibility with the operations staff) Serve as a back-up for admissions material inventory Serve as a back-up to generate and assemble admission decision packets for admitted students, including printing letters, certificates, and envelopes, and assist with the packaging of decision materials as needed Assist in the hiring process for Admissions Clerical Assistants (ACAs) Other duties as assigned Schedule: Regular hours will be Monday – Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. (12-month position). Minimum Qualifications High school diploma (or equivalent) required; Associate’s Degree in related field or a minimum of three (3) years experience in a high volume office environment with a focus on customer service required Excellent time management and organizational skills, and the ability to manage multiple responsibilities and prioritize tasks Strong communication skills Ability to work independently and as a member of a team Ability to handle stressful situations and to work in an active, sometimes noisy office environment Ability to adapt to changing priorities and to switch tasks on short notice Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Outlook, Teams) Preferred Qualifications Experience working with Slate by Technolutions Experience working in higher education Ability to learn and adopt new technologies quickly and thoroughly Familiarity with the North Country and our local area Data entry experience A positive, goal-oriented mindset Salary CSEA Level 15, $18.77 - $25.68.The actual compensation will be determined based on experience and other factors permitted by law. Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) Full-time (12 months) Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01540 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Please complete application form and include contact information for at least three professional work references. Upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section. All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Reference Letters 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4596": {
      "title": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Utility - 11 Month Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Utility - 11 Month Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the on-line application form and provide a minimum of three professional references with names and phone numbers. Upload a resume and cover letter in the “Applicant Documents” section of the application. All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of a background check (including criminal record) Posting Details Position Information Position Title Utility - 11 Month FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Responsibilities Under direct supervision, performs a variety of tasks concerned with the sanitation, maintenance and upkeep of a Dining Services Unit. On occasion, as required, performs the primary duties of other A classification personnel as assigned by the Management staff. In addition to the requirements for personal conduct which are common to all positions in the University, the following duties outline the major factors of the position. They are not all inclusive, do not set a priority sequence, or establish a ration of work to be performed. They may vary in importance between departments and may be altered within the general framework of the primary function to satisfy changes in departmental activity. Cleans garbage cans and properly disposes of garbage, trash and recyclables. Cleans and maintains utility rooms, loading docks and trash areas. Cleans and polishes dining service equipment, fixtures and furniture. Transports and stores dishes, utensils, equipment and supplies to the proper stations and/or storage areas. Washes, mops, cleans, waxes and maintains ceilings, walls, floors, windows, equipment and furniture in the Dining Service Unit. Maintains kitchen and public areas, dining rooms, lobbies and restrooms in the Dining Services Unit. Operates the dish washing machine, including cleaning the machine according to schedule. Performs hand dishwashing. Washes and maintains hoods, vents, ducts, filters and grease traps. Maintains correct standards of cleanliness and safety. Contributes to the total function of the dining service operation. Performs other related duties as assigned. Schedule: Friday – Tuesday 2:30pm – 10:30pm Days Off: Wednesday and Thursday Location: Dana Dining Hall Minimum Qualifications High School diploma or equivalent required. Must have the ability to operate mechanical cleaning devices and to correctly measure, weigh, and apply simple cleaning solutions. Move 25 lbs. or more a distance of 10 ft or more. Develop positive and productive working relationships. Effectively present information and respond to questions from managers, customers, co-workers, and the campus community Support a positive work environment through teamwork, honesty, approachability, and a commitment to customer service. Must be able to meet the university’s requirement to be authorized to drive a university vehicle. Preferred Qualifications Salary SEIU Level A: $16.00 to $21.38/hr. The actual compensation will be determined based on experience and other factors permitted by law. Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) FT Seasonal Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01517 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Please complete the on-line application form and provide a minimum of three professional references with names and phone numbers. Upload a resume and cover letter in the “Applicant Documents” section of the application. All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of a background check (including criminal record) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Reference Letters 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4550": {
      "title": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Concessions Crew Member Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Concessions Crew Member Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application form and include contact information for at least three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. SLU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Concessions Crew Member FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Responsibilities Take customer orders and assemble them correctly. Check identification for age-restricted items, such as alcoholic beverages. Accept payment from customers via a cash register. Check food items to ensure quality and safety standards are met. Keep the assigned area clean, sanitary, and safe. Perform basic maintenance on machines and equipment, as needed. Answer questions about concession stand location, prices of goods sold there, and other questions about tickets or other items sold. Under the guidance of a supervisor, maintain concession stand records with information on products used and food served to customers. Complete inventory sheets daily, noting supplies that need to be replenished. Enter data into a computerized cash register system. They may also be responsible for balancing register tills at the end of day. ‍ These are temporary work opportunities and primary work hours are on Fridays and Saturdays during the Ice Hockey Season. Additional hours may be possible during the week based on needs. Work hours are part-time, flexible shifts, and include day, evening, and weekends. Minimum Qualifications Positive customer service skills and ability to read, write, and follow directions required. Ability to operate a cash register and standard cooking and dish washing equipment as well as ability to work with chemicals for cleaning required. Must be 16 years of age, or older. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience is helpful, but not required. Salary $16.00/hr. Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) PT Seasonal Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01519 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Please complete the online application form and include contact information for at least three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. SLU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4439": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant Coach",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant Coach - Men&#39;s &amp; Women&#39;s Crew Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Graduate Assistant Coach - Men's & Women's Crew Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested and qualified applicants should complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Nick Hughes, Head Coach, at nhughes@stlawu.edu. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Assistant Coach - Men's & Women's Crew FLSA Exempt Primary Responsibilities St. Lawrence University is currently seeking applications for a Graduate Assistant Coach for Men’s & Women’s Crew. This is a 9-month position (August 2026 – May 2027) targeted toward graduate students seeking a master’s degree. Remuneration includes a competitive coaching stipend, student health insurance, and eligibility for tuition remission (6 graduate classes per year in the University’s graduate program). St Lawrence offers a Master of Arts in Leadership. Duties/Responsibilities Responsibilities include providing instruction and assisting in practice preparation, race day duties, recruiting, and administrative tasks as assigned by the Head Coach. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree is required. Strong oral and written communication skills. Valid driver’s license and ability to meet the requirements to drive University vehicles required. Apply and be accepted in the graduate program at St. Lawrence University. Preferred Qualifications Collegiate rowing and/or coaching experience preferred. Salary $888 biweekly Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) FT Seasonal Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01474 Desired Start Date 08/10/2026 Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicant Interested and qualified applicants should complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Nick Hughes, Head Coach, at nhughes@stlawu.edu. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree or higher? Yes No * Do you hold a valid driver's license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Contact Information for 3 Professional References Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4631": {
      "title": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Catering Crew Member (Temp) Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Catering Crew Member (Temp) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. - Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until position is filled. - Please complete the online application and provide three professional references with names and phone numbers. - Position is temp only Posting Details Employment Position Title Catering Crew Member (Temp) Primary Responsibilities Under the supervision of the Catering Manager and unit supervisory staff, the catering FSG is responsible for the many aspects of preparation for and execution of a special function, especially VIP functions. This includes equipment, dishes, condition of the linen, assisting in food preparation, function set-up and clean-up, customer service during the event, etc. Must maintain a high level of professionalism and customer service. This is a full-time, seasonal position. Biweekly work schedules are created and are determined by scheduled events; schedules may vary. Primary Duties include: Check and review the special functions, present and future. Develop a list of dishes and equipment needed for each function. Gather all listed items, plus linen for the function, check quality and cleanliness. Maintain linen inventory. Check status of production – advise management and supervisory staff. Communicate effectively with all catering and unit staff. Assist in food production. Assist in food and equipment delivery. Set-up function, including linen, table settings, buffet presentation, etc. Guide and supervise waitstaff in preparation, service and clean up. Assist in customer service during the event to include table service, buffet replenishing, beverage and bar services, etc. Clear function and return event location to pre-function condition. Assist in loading, unloading and storage of food and equipment following the event. Help coordinate and train temporary staff. Responsible for performing regular unit Food Service Generalist duties. Supervision Received: General supervision by unit supervisory staff and Catering Manager. Supervision Given: May coordinate and train temporary student waitstaff. Schedule: will be driven by event requests, can and will include nights, weekends, holidays. Average number of hours weekly: 20 Minimum Qualifications HS diploma (or equivalent) required. One to two years of catering and/or upscale dining & waiting experience. Ability to properly wait on tables and serve correctly, lift 20 pounds, stand and walk for several hours at a time. Must be detail oriented. Follow and use food production equipment, dish washing and other mechanical devices. Contributes to the total function of the dining services operation in a positive manner. Must be able to meet university requirements to serve alcohol. Must meet the university’s requirements to be authorized to drive a university vehicle. Preferred Qualifications • Develop positive and productive working relationships • Effectively present information and respond to questions from managers, customers, co-workers and the campus community • Support a positive work environment through teamwork honesty, approachable and a commitment to customer service. Salary Range $16.00/hr. Appointment Timing Less than six (6) months Posting Detail Information Posting Number AT00108 Desired Start Date Position End Date Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant - Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until position is filled. - Please complete the online application and provide three professional references with names and phone numbers. - Position is temp only Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4606": {
      "title": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Food Service Generalist Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Food Service Generalist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. SLU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Food Service Generalist FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Responsibilities PURPOSE & PRIMARY FUNCTION Under the supervision of Leader, Assistant Managers and Managers is responsible for food preparation and general kitchen duties. DUTIES PERFORMED In addition to the requirements for personal conduct which are common to all positions in the University, the following duties outline the major factors of the position. They are not all inclusive, do not set a priority sequence, or establish a ration of work to be performed. They may vary in importance between departments and may be altered within the general framework of the primary function to satisfy changes in departmental activity. Prepares food items, according to documented recipes in the area assigned and continues to monitor food quality throughout the meal periods. Responsible for all condiments and garnishes for the meal in assigned area. Responsible for replenishing and maintaining area assigned. Assures proper temperatures and HACCP conditions on serving lines and/or in areas assigned. Prepares items and performs the necessary tasks required for catered functions as assigned. Maintains standards of good personnel relations with guests and co-workers. Responsible for maintaining a clean, sanitary and safe work area, following the established standards. Operates cash registers according to established procedures and assists in preparing assigned reports. Checks in meal tickets and accepts cash for meals and purchases and maintains safety and security of dining areas. Responsible for serving the customers in an efficient and courteous manner. Work in the dish room and washes dishes, pots and pans, plus any assigned foodservice equipment. Clean equipment, freezer, refrigerators, storerooms and general kitchen areas. Prepare and complete forms and reports, as requested. Participate in recipe testing and development. Contributes to the total function of the dining service operation in a positive manner. Training and guidance with instructions for temporary employees who work with them. Performs other duties as assigned These are full-time, nine month positions in accordance with the academic year and with full benefits packages including health, dental, tuition free classes, free access to a fitness center and sporting events and a retirement match! Schedule is: Sun. – Thursday 2:30 – 10:30pm Days off: Friday and Saturday Location: North Star Cafe Minimum Qualifications High School diploma (or equivalent) required. Prior experience is preferred. Ability to operate cash register, standard cooking and dish washing equipment and other mechanical devices located in a food service operation. Preferred Qualifications Prior food service experience is preferred. Salary SEIU Level B $16.13 - $21.90. The actual compensation will be determined based on experience and other factors permitted by law. Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) FT Seasonal Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01476 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Please complete the online application form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. SLU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4557": {
      "title": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Dining Services Crew Members - Academic Year 2026 - 2027 (Temp) Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Dining Services Crew Members - Academic Year 2026 - 2027 (Temp) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application form and include contact information for professional references. You must be at least 16 years of age to be considered for temporary positions at St. Lawrence University. St. Lawrence University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Posting Details Employment Position Title Dining Services Crew Members - Academic Year 2026 - 2027 (Temp) Primary Responsibilities Opportunity to work several shifts/week (up to 20 hours) in one (or more) of the University’s dining units. Work includes assisting with food prep and staffing a variety of food stations within the units, cleaning, stocking, and dish washing. Wage rate = $16.00/hour Work hours are part-time, flexible shifts and include day, evening, and weekends. Minimum Qualifications Positive customer service skills and ability to read, write, and follow directions required. Ability to operate standard cooking and dish washing equipment as well as ability to work with chemicals for cleaning required. Must be 16 years of age, or older. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience is helpful, but not required. Salary Range $16.00/hr. Appointment Timing Less than six (6) months Posting Detail Information Posting Number AT00112 Desired Start Date Position End Date Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Please complete the online application form and include contact information for professional references. You must be at least 16 years of age to be considered for temporary positions at St. Lawrence University. St. Lawrence University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.stlawu.edu/postings/4510": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Safety and Security",
      "description": "St. Lawrence University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Director of Safety and Security Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging Dual Careers Assistant Director of Safety and Security Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested and qualified applicants please complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Director of Safety and Security FLSA Exempt Primary Responsibilities Reporting to the Director of Safety and Security, this position is responsible for the leadership and supervision of departmental staff in providing a safe and secure environment for all community members, as well as all University property. The Assistant Director shares in the supervision of a professional staff consisting of: three sergeants, five security officers, one emergency dispatcher, the Student Safety Team, and the First Response Team. The Assistant Director’s work schedule will typically be assigned to night shifts and most weekends or be determined by the Director of Safety & Security in support of the department operations. The Assistant Director position will be responsible for overseeing critical investigations, both internal and criminal for the Safety & Security Department. In addition, the employee will be responsible for the Safety & Security component of compliance and investigations for a variety of laws, regulations and mandates. These regulations include Title IX, Clery, VAWA (Violence Against Women Act, NYS Education Law including sections 129A and 129B (Enough is Enough 7/15). The employee will be expected to assist in developing emergency plans, periodically provide off-hours supervision at key events, and participate in the on-call Safety & Security administrator duties. Campus Life Assists in providing leadership and vision in securing a safe university environment. Works closely with the sergeants, security officers and emergency dispatchers in insuring that all university policies are enforced and procedures/protocols are followed. Works closely with the Director to ensure that all appropriate staff training and development is provided. Assist in the responsibility for ensuring that every sergeant and security officer meets the New York State Security Guard Act’s annual training requirements. Crisis Management Assists in overseeing crisis training of all sergeants, security officers and emergency dispatchers in an effort to insure that emergency policies and protocols are in place and are being followed. Develops a close working relationship with the Department of Residence Life, Facilities Operations, the local Police and Fire/ EMS agencies. In case of any emergency situation the Assistant Director will support the Director of Safety and Security in assuming on-site command and control. Staff Supervision Provides first line supervision for three sergeants, five security officers, one emergency dispatcher, the Student Safety Team and the First Response Team. Works with the Director to ensure appropriate outcomes relative to departmental complaints, personnel complaints, disagreements and appeals. On-call Supervisor when designated by the Director of Safety and Security. Coordination with Other Campus Entities Actively participates and contributes to the Student Life team. Collaborates with the Office of Intercultural Engagement, Inclusion, and Belonging and Student Life to share insights on operations and training of staff. Works collaboratively with university departments on event staffing requests. Serves on a variety of committees. Works closely with the Information Technology, Facilities Operations and Health & Counseling. Minimum Qualifications Associates degree required. Equivalent combination of education and experience will be considered. Two to three years of experience at a supervisory level, in the field of campus security, including patrol, investigation, supervision, training, and administration. Must have experience working with a variety of people and ability to communicate successfully with young adults, faculty, and staff. NYS Security Guard License required. Valid driver’s license, good driving history and meet university standards for driving. Pass a detailed background check. Preferred Qualifications Experience in law enforcement preferred. Salary Salary range $68,000 to $75,000 annually Status (FT, PT, Seasonal, Temp) Full-time (12 months) Posting Detail Information Posting Number ST01501 Desired Start Date Open Date (to accept applications) Close Date (date applications will not be considered) Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Interested and qualified applicants please complete the online application form and upload required documents in the “applicant documents” section of the form. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All offers of employment are contingent upon the finalist successfully passing a background (including criminal records) check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Contact Information for 3 Professional References Optional Documents Additional Document 1 23 Romoda Dr. Canton, New York, 13617 Back to top Copyright © St. Lawrence University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
